      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not support the general claim that a neurosignature is “a characteristic pattern of brain-network activity or connectivity associated with a condition or process”; it only describes a “potential neurosignature” in the context of fibromyalgia (FM) and major depressive disorder (MDD) and overlapping mechanisms.",
        "The wording “may show both shared disruption in pain and emotion regulation systems” is only partially supported: the packet refers to “shared disruptions in pain and emotion regulation networks,” not “systems.”",
        "The definition’s broader formulation that it “refers to a pattern” with implications beyond the specific FM vs MDD context is not directly established in the packet, which only discusses overlapping and distinct neural mechanisms between those conditions."
